  "contract": {
    "extraction": "The model transcribes grade, quote kind, original unit and amount from dealer text. Validate its JSON with Zod before normalizing. Emit recognized grades in grade_order. A list header applies to its entries. All sample prices use INR.",
    "missing_prices": "Omitted grades yield no row. An explicit unchanged or relative-to-yesterday statement needs yesterday’s close for that grade. Keep unpriced or ambiguous mentions with a reason. Hold unresolved grades, units, pricing tiers and unreadable amounts for review.",
    "precision": "Normalize prices server-side using fixed-scale decimal arithmetic. Divide INR per metric tonne by 1000. PostgreSQL stores metal rates and thresholds as NUMERIC(14,4). The examples fit to two places, so their JSON strings and Telegram amounts display two.",
    "persistence": "Insert material_grade, rate_per_kg, source and recorded_at. The database sets previous_rate_per_kg from the chronological predecessor and generates change_delta. In these independent cases the predecessor is yesterday’s close.",
    "trigger": "For each chat, match an active alert_rules row by grade. Compare the absolute DB-generated change_delta with threshold_rs_per_kg, including equality. A missing predecessor yields no alert. should_notify is true if any grade triggers for that chat.",
    "deduplication": "Collapse identical repeated quotes per grade. Distinct conflicting quotes for the same grade require review. On retry, reuse the source_channel, source_conversation_id and source_message_id tuple to prevent a duplicate rate or alert.",
    "telegram": "Format only the triggered grades in grade_order. Each grade shows its new rate and signed change in INR/kg. Place at most two grades on each rate line. A null expected_telegram_text means zero sends."
  },
